body:
@speller26 for visibility. Thanks @ryanhill1 for raising this. The main issue is that without the verbatim box, the submitted circuit is treated as a virtual one, i.e. you are requesting a 54 qubit register, which will not always be available. IQM happens to disable qubits which are not well calibrated, so occasionally you have less than 54 qubits (right now Q46 is missing, so you have 53 available qubits - you can check this with `len(emerald.properties.standardized.oneQubitProperties)`, or by looking in the AWS Console on the calibration tab). 

If you want to target the physical qubits, you just modify the above code as `device.run(Circuit().add_verbatim_box(ghz),shots=100)`, and it should work. You'll run into connectivity issues, but not the qubit ones. 

Please let us know if this resolves the issue!
